# 43. WHAT TO DO WITH THE CURRENT 170 MODULES

Do not attempt to make all 170 modules green simultaneously.

For every module:

1. identify its business importance;
2. identify upstream dependencies;
3. identify downstream consumers;
4. determine whether it is operational or configuration-only;
5. determine whether its current fail-closed state is correct;
6. determine whether it can safely be implemented;
7. implement only when its contract is known;
8. test it;
9. test its failure behavior;
10. test authorization;
11. test concurrency where relevant;
12. test persistence;
13. test downstream effects;
14. test recovery;
15. update its evidence status.

If a module cannot yet be implemented correctly, do not fake it.

